# Source-Scoped Question Drafts and Immutable Ask

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: A1 Local question state
Dependencies: 27_AI_ANSWER_RESEARCH.todo

## Purpose

Choose a dictated or typed question without accidentally sending the rest of a meeting.

## Tasks

- [ ] Add a bounded structured transcript store with capture-session/source/segment/epoch/revision identity.
- [ ] Preserve existing source-labelled display/export and all prior transcript tests.
- [ ] Build an editable local QuestionDraft from explicit selected segments, an armed Mic span or typed text.
- [ ] Do not infer provenance by parsing rendered `[Mic]` labels or copy the entire transcript.
- [ ] Freeze exactly the displayed draft/revision on Ask, including its provisional/final provenance.
- [ ] Define empty/oversized input, multi-segment questions, user edits and late ASR revision behavior.
- [ ] Keep Computer text out of a Mic draft unless the owner explicitly selects it.
- [ ] Add deterministic source/session/revision/cancel/eviction tests with synthetic data.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Only explicit Ask creates an outbound request; natural finals/question marks never auto-send.
- [ ] Submitted snapshots are immutable; later transcript text cannot rewrite or resend them.
- [ ] Prior unrelated Mic text and all unselected Computer/notes/chat data stay out of the prompt.
- [ ] No new recording-permission or recipient-rehearsal confirmation is introduced.

## Completion evidence

- 2026-10-08 17:37 owner authorized the next ready implementation after the book offload.
- Local structured selection/typed drafts and immutable snapshots are being implemented; no Azure calls.
- Armed live-Mic start/end boundaries depend on negotiated commit29; do not pretend v2 partial text provides sample-exact cuts.

